<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6893" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carthaea</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καρθαία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town on the south coast of the Cycladic
				island Ceos</i> or <i>Cea</i>, now <i>Poles</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 20, §
			62</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carthēus</span></b>  and
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carthēĭus</span></b> , a, um, <i>Carthœan</i>, <i>of
				Carthœa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 109</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenia = Carthaea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 7, 368</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
